Ques6:
You need to measure the average temperature of a classroom using only one sensor. Where would you place the sensor and why? Explain how 
poor placement could affect the accuracy of your measurements. Assume the classroom to be a square-base cuboid of side length “a” and height“b”. 
Ans – I would place the sensor at the center of the classroom at about 1.5 meters above the floor. It should be away from windows, doors, 
fans, and ACs because these can affect the temperature reading. This position gives the most accurate average temperature of the room.
